 "address_en_source": "machine_translation",
 "category": "historic",
 "category_zh": "历史遗址",
 "category_en": "Historic site",
 "intro_zh": "清东陵位于河北省遵化市境内，是我国现存体系最完整、布局最得体的帝王陵墓建筑群。主要景点有孝陵、景陵、裕陵、慈禧陵、慈安陵、昭西陵、裕妃园寝等。2000年被列入《世界文化遗产名录》。",
 "intro_en": "The Eastern Qing tombs (Chinese: 清東陵; pinyin: Qīng Dōng líng; Manchu: ᡩᡝᡵᡤᡳ ᡝᡵᡤᡳ ᠮᡠᠩᡤᠠᠨ, romanized: dergi ergi munggan) are an imperial mausoleum complex of the Qing dynasty located in Zunhua county of Tangshan in Hebei province, 125 kilometres (78 mi) northeast of Beijing. They are the largest, most complete, and best preserved extant mausoleum complex in China. Altogether, five emperors (Shunzhi, Kangxi, Qianlong, Xianfeng, and Tongzhi), 15 empresses, 136 imperial concubines, three princes, and two princesses of the Qing dynasty are buried here. Surrounded by Changrui Mountain, Jinxing Mountain, Huanghua Mountain, and Yingfei Daoyang Mountain, the tomb complex stretches over a total area of 80 square kilometres (31 sq mi).",
 "intro_en_source": "wikipedia",
